Subject: [PATCH] fix(display): probe the brightness clamp from the service itself

The 0001 patch only shows its value when the two fields of the request line can
disagree, and they can only disagree for an out-of-range request:
K60BacklightCodec.h clampLevel() maps anything >= kMaxLevel (2047) onto 2047
and anything <= 0 onto 0. A slider never sends that, so a flight that merely
drags the slider produces lines whose two fields are equal - the log is
untouched by the defect and the patch looks pointless.

This adds the smallest thing that makes the question answerable on the device
without waiting for the OS to misbehave: with k60_backlight_probe=1 the service
asks itself, once, for level 4095 - the top of the panel's own 12 bit DBV
domain, the value a caller would pass if it mistook DBV units for levels. With
0001 applied that prints exactly one line

    K60 BACKLIGHT: brightness level 4095 -> level 2047 dbv 0xfff

and without 0001 it prints 2047 twice, which is the defect itself.

Off by default: the argument is the only way in, nothing in the image sets it,
and the cost of turning it on is one visible jump to full brightness at
bring-up before user space takes over. The probe is stacked on 0001 and is
never shipped alone - alone it can only reprint the clamped value.

Criteria and the reading rules: docs/research/display/BACKLIGHT-LOG-CRITERIA.md.
Applies to the 27 ladder branch only.
---
--- a/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
+++ b/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
@@ -379,6 +379,31 @@ void K60Backlight::publishFirst(void)
           (int)native_backlight_request[0], (int)native_backlight_request[1],
           (int)native_backlight_request[4], (int)native_backlight_request[5],
           control ? "" : " (no AppleARMBacklight conformance)");
+
+    /* k60_backlight_probe=1: ask ourselves the question a flight cannot wait
+     * for. The clamp path (K60BacklightCodec.h clampLevel) only separates the
+     * two fields of the "brightness level" line when the request is out of
+     * range, and no UI sends 4095 - it is the top of the panel's own 12 bit
+     * DBV domain (kMaxDbv 0xfff), not a level. With 0001 applied this prints
+     * exactly one line before user space takes over:
+     *
+     *   K60 BACKLIGHT: brightness level 4095 -> level 2047 dbv 0xfff
+     *
+     * Without 0001 both fields read 2047 (the defect being measured), so the
+     * probe is stacked on that patch, never alone. Off by default; the
+     * argument is the only way in, and the side effect is one visible jump to
+     * full brightness at bring-up. */
+    uint32_t probe = 0;
+    if (bootArg("k60_backlight_probe", probe) && probe) {
+        OSDictionary *request = OSDictionary::withCapacity(1);
+        OSNumber *outOfRange = OSNumber::withNumber(4095ULL, 32);
+        if (request) {
+            if (outOfRange) request->setObject("brightness", outOfRange);
+            setProperties(request);
+            request->release();
+        }
+        if (outOfRange) outOfRange->release();
+    }
 }
 
 IOReturn K60Backlight::setProperties(OSObject *properties)
